Requirements: 29   with obligations: 28   deliberately none: 1

[task-01] A review completes and reports even when some of its criteria are ones no test
    could ever evidence.
    -> review-completes-and-reports-with-no-evidence-criteria  [functional/explicit]
       A review completes and reports even when some of its criteria are ones no test
       could ever evidence.
    -> no-test-can-evidence-criterion-statement-supported  [functional/inferred]
       A criterion may be answered with a statement that no test can evidence it.
    -> statement-does-not-abort-review  [functional/explicit]   (also serves constraint-03)
       A criterion answered with such a statement does not abort the review.
    -> review-produces-report-when-all-weak-criteria-have-no-test-evidence-statements  [functional/explicit]   (also serves constraint-07)
       A review in which every weak criterion is answered with a statement that no test
       can evidence it produces a report.

[constraint-01] A test recommendation may state that no test can evidence its criterion.
    -> recommendation-may-state-no-test-can-evidence  [functional/explicit]
       A test recommendation may state that no test can evidence its criterion.

[constraint-02] A statement that no test can evidence a criterion carries a reason.
    -> statement-carries-reason  [functional/explicit]
       A statement that no test can evidence a criterion carries a reason.

[constraint-03] A criterion answered with such a statement does not abort the review.
    -> statement-does-not-abort-review  [functional/explicit]   (also serves task-01)
       A criterion answered with such a statement does not abort the review.

[constraint-04] A criterion for which the model returns neither a recommendation nor
    such a statement still aborts the review.
    -> missing-answer-still-aborts-review  [functional/explicit]
       A criterion for which the model returns neither a recommendation nor such a
       statement still aborts the review.

[constraint-05] A statement that no test can evidence a criterion is recorded in the
    persisted review state.
    -> statement-recorded-in-persisted-review-state  [functional/explicit]
       A statement that no test can evidence a criterion is recorded in the persisted
       review state.

[constraint-06] A recorded statement of that kind names the criterion it applies to.
    -> recorded-statement-names-criterion  [functional/explicit]
       A recorded statement of that kind names the criterion it applies to.

[constraint-07] A review in which every weak criterion is answered that way produces a
    report.
    -> review-produces-report-when-all-weak-criteria-have-no-test-evidence-statements  [functional/explicit]   (also serves task-01)
       A review in which every weak criterion is answered with a statement that no test
       can evidence it produces a report.

[constraint-08] A criterion that the change addresses and that carries such a statement
    is classified as indeterminate on the test-evidence axis.
    -> criterion-with-no-test-evidence-statement-is-indeterminate-on-test-evidence-axis  [functional/explicit]
       A criterion that the change addresses and that carries a statement that no test
       can evidence it is classified as indeterminate on the test-evidence axis.

[constraint-09] The report distinguishes a criterion for which no test was recommended
    because none can evidence it from a criterion for which no test was recommended.
    -> report-distinguishes-no-test-evidence-from-no-recommendation  [functional/explicit]
       The report distinguishes a criterion for which no test was recommended because
       none can evidence it from a criterion for which no test was not recommended.

[constraint-10] A review of a change that modifies only configuration files produces a
    report.
    -> config-only-change-produces-report  [functional/explicit]
       A review of a change that modifies only configuration files produces a report.

[constraint-11] Two runs over the same criteria and the same change produce the same
    statements that no test can evidence them.
    -> same-inputs-produce-same-no-test-evidence-statements  [invariant/explicit]
       Two runs over the same criteria and the same change produce the same statements
       that no test can evidence them.

[constraint-12] A recorded model exchange carries the reason the model stopped
    generating.
    -> recorded-model-exchange-carries-stop-reason  [functional/explicit]
       A recorded model exchange carries the reason the model stopped generating.

[exclusion-01] Whether the existing exclusion of criteria whose evidence is code alone
    is folded into the same mechanism.
    -> scope-exclusion-existing-code-only-evidence-folding  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not alter whether the existing exclusion of criteria whose
       evidence is code alone is folded into the same mechanism.

[exclusion-02] How many criteria are carried in one recommendation request.
    -> scope-exclusion-recommendation-request-batch-size  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not alter how many criteria are carried in one recommendation
       request.

[exclusion-03] Whether the model's judgement that no test can evidence a criterion is
    correct.
    -> model-judgement-correctness-out-of-scope  [human_review/explicit]
       The change does not address whether the model's judgement that no test can
       evidence a criterion is correct.

[exclusion-04] How a criterion's test evidence is classified as weak in the first place.
    -> weakness-classification-out-of-scope  [human_review/explicit]
       The change does not address how a criterion's test evidence is classified as weak
       in the first place.

[exclusion-05] How the overall completion verdict is derived for criteria that carry no
    such statement.
    -> overall-completion-verdict-out-of-scope  [human_review/explicit]
       The change does not address how the overall completion verdict is derived for
       criteria that carry no such statement.

[exclusion-06] Recommending non-test evidence in place of the test that cannot exist.
    -> non-test-evidence-recommendation-out-of-scope  [human_review/explicit]
       The change does not address recommending non-test evidence in place of the test
       that cannot exist.

[completion-01] Implementation
    -- no obligation, deliberately
       This is a section marker standing alone with no requirement under it.

[completion-02] A test asserts that a criterion answered with a statement that no test
    can evidence it does not abort the review.
    -> test-criterion-statement-does-not-abort-review  [test_demand/explicit]
       A test asserts that a criterion answered with a statement that no test can
       evidence it does not abort the review.

[completion-03] A test asserts that a criterion the model omits entirely still aborts
    the review.
    -> test-omitted-criterion-still-aborts-review  [test_demand/explicit]
       A test asserts that a criterion the model omits entirely still aborts the review.

[completion-04] A test asserts that such a statement reaches the persisted review state
    attributed to its criterion.
    -> test-statement-reaches-persisted-state-attributed-to-criterion  [test_demand/explicit]
       A test asserts that such a statement reaches the persisted review state
       attributed to its criterion.

[completion-05] A test asserts that a review whose weak criteria are all answered that
    way produces a report.
    -> test-all-weak-criteria-answered-that-way-produce-report  [test_demand/explicit]
       A test asserts that a review whose weak criteria are all answered that way
       produces a report.

[completion-06] A test asserts that an addressed criterion carrying such a statement is
    classified indeterminate on the test-evidence axis.
    -> test-addressed-criterion-classified-indeterminate-on-test-evidence-axis  [test_demand/explicit]
       A test asserts that an addressed criterion carrying such a statement is
       classified indeterminate on the test-evidence axis.

[completion-07] A test asserts that the report renders a criterion no test can evidence
    differently from a criterion with no recommendation.
    -> test-report-renders-no-test-can-evidence-differently-from-no-recommendation  [test_demand/explicit]
       A test asserts that the report renders a criterion no test can evidence
       differently from a criterion with no recommendation.

[completion-08] A test asserts that a review of a change modifying only configuration
    files produces a report.
    -> test-config-only-change-produces-report  [test_demand/explicit]
       A test asserts that a review of a change modifying only configuration files
       produces a report.

[completion-09] A test asserts that two runs over the same criteria and change produce
    the same statements.
    -> test-two-runs-same-statements  [test_demand/explicit]
       A test asserts that two runs over the same criteria and change produce the same
       statements.

[completion-10] A test asserts that a recorded model exchange carries the reason the
    model stopped generating.
    -> test-recorded-model-exchange-reason  [test_demand/explicit]
       A test asserts that a recorded model exchange carries the reason the model
       stopped generating.

